<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mamilia gens</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mamilii</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mamilia gens was a family of Tusculum in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latium">Latium</a> that later became part of the Roman nobility. Its legendary leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/octavius-mamilius">Octavius Mamilius</a> was the son-in-law of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarquinius-superbus">Tarquinius Superbus</a> and is said to have led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latins</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> at Lake Regillus around 496 BCE. The family later gained Roman citizenship, and Lucius Mamilius Vitulus, consul in 265 BCE, was the first of several of its members to hold the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">consulship</a>.</p></div>
